-- Approval limits - the smallest worked example exercising the
-- decimal-comparison primitive (v0).
--
-- Domain: extends Example 6 (actor authority) with *quantitative*
-- authority. Where Example 6 says "this actor may approve documents
-- of this kind", Example 7 says "this actor may approve documents
-- of this kind up to this amount". The shape is the natural one a
-- business uses: a clerk approves expenses up to £1,000; a manager
-- up to £10,000; a controller up to £100,000.
--
-- The forcing question: how do you say "amount <= limit" without
-- smuggling the comparison through equality games or extending the
-- aggregation sublanguage? `Expr::Le` is added in this PR as the
-- single decimal-comparison primitive in the IR. `Lt`, `Gt`, `Ge`
-- arrive when an example forces them; for approval ceilings, `<=`
-- is what the business says.
--
-- No invariants. Same require-vs-invariant doctrine as Example 6:
-- revoking a limit does not retroactively invalidate an approval
-- that was admitted while the limit was in force.


transformation grant_approval_limit(actor, doc_type, limit):
    assert ApprovalLimit(actor, doc_type, limit)
    emit ApprovalLimitGranted(actor, doc_type, limit)


transformation revoke_approval_limit(actor, doc_type, limit):
    require ApprovalLimit(actor, doc_type, limit)
    retract ApprovalLimit(actor, doc_type, limit)
    emit ApprovalLimitRevoked(actor, doc_type, limit)


-- The transformation declares no `actor` parameter. The actor flows
-- through transition context and is read via $actor (Term::Actor).
--
-- The require binds `limit` from an ApprovalLimit claim about the
-- proposing actor and then compares it to the proposed amount via
-- `<=`. A document worth 750 against a 1000 limit admits; one worth
-- 1001 does not. At-the-boundary equality (amount == limit) admits.
transformation approve_within_limit(doc_id, doc_type, amount):
    require ApprovalLimit($actor, doc_type, limit) and amount <= limit
    assert LimitedApproval(doc_id, doc_type, amount, $actor)
    emit DocumentApprovedWithinLimit(doc_id, $actor, amount)
